  "notes": [
    "Equal-output checks; three query samples with no timing assertions. A Debug lake integration build ran concurrently, so timings are illustrative.",
    "Compact probe blocks borrow a forward reader arena, capped at 16 KiB retention, until every match for the current probe row drains. A reusable row buffer avoids per-row allocations.",
    "The 100k-row spilled join fixture uses 370435-370436 backing allocations versus 397116 at the pushed dictionary checkpoint (about 6.7% fewer); the earlier compact-typed-state baseline remains slightly lower at 365596-365597.",
    "Peak allocation is unchanged for the complete join fixture; this measurement does not establish lower whole-query memory or remote index serving.",
    "Tests cover duplicate matches, exact payloads, SQL NULL versus JSON null, early close, mixed singleton and typed records, rewind, and allocation failure propagation."
